	<Item Name="GDS" Type="String" />
	<Item Name="title" Type="String">A kinome-wide CRISPR screen identifies CK1&#945; as a novel target to overcome enzalutamide resistance of prostate cancer</Item>
	<Item Name="summary" Type="String">Utilizing a kinome-wide CRISPR-Cas9 knockout screen, we identified casein kinase 1 alpha (CK1&#945;) as a novel therapeutic target to overcome enzalutamide resistance. To dissect the underlying mechanisms of targeting CK1&#945; to sensitize cancer cells to ENZA, we performed RNA sequencing of 22Rv1 cells upon CK1&#945; knockout or overexpression. We found that CK1&#945; regulated double-strand break (DSB)-response signaling.</Item>
